// HumanityOS home design: the HOMESTEAD FOR ONE (21 x 34 m plot, one person, one storey).
// Approved by the operator 2026-11-13 (docs/design/home-room-program.md, section 5 and "His
// answers": "Make them one room" for the living room, kitchen and dining). A start of its own
// (data/homes/starts.ron); today's homestead stays the default until the wipe decides.
//
// FRAME. Home-local metres from the box's min corner, x east, z south. The street is WEST (x < 0):
// plots of this kind stand on the east side of First Street (data/blueprints/ship_structure.ron),
// the door in the west wall. Drawn with the street at the top (`node scripts/draw-homes.js
// <folder>`), the plan reads as the approved draft: data x is the distance from the street, data z
// is 21 less the distance along the street.
//
// THE PLAN, street first: the front path and drive (x 0..2); the HOUSE (x 2..8, z 10..21): shower
// room 2.5 x 3.5 m, bedroom and desk 3.5 x 3.5 m (12.25 m2, over England's 11.5 m2 double), the
// living, kitchen and dining room 6 x 5 m, and the entry and utility 6 x 2.5 m, a through-room from
// the front door to the garden door; the side path (z 8..10) and the WORKSHOP AND VEHICLE BAY
// (8 x 8 m, its folding door on the drive); the back terrace; the garden path; the GREENHOUSE
// (x 10..18, 144 m2 of growing floor) with the harvest store and the mushroom room; then the
// ORCHARD and beds, six hens with their hen house, a pair of rabbits, the compost and a hive
// (x 18..34).
//
// WALLS, LIDS AND WHAT THIS SHAPE CANNOT HOLD YET: as data/homes/household_homestead.ron says.
// The bedroom keeps its window to the terrace; its side window would be in the plot's shell.
//
// Materials: 0 = grid, 1 = steel/metal, 2 = concrete, 3 = wood, 4 = glass, 6 = pine.

